{
  "raw": {
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a78839ea0f4259801a112d1777e3f1f": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Psychology Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1022 # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Psychology Coe College, a small liberal arts college of 1,200 students in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, seeks qualified applicants for a full-time tenure-track appointment in Psychology . The successful candidate will have a specialization in behavioral or cognitive neuroscience. The successful candidate will teach a 3:3 load, including regularly teaching Biopsychology and upper-level neuroscience courses. Additional courses may include Introductory Psychology, Statistics, a first- year seminar and/or upper-level seminar course in an area of interest to the candidate. The Department is committed to a student-centered perspective and an inclusive approach to teaching and research. A doctoral degree is required by the start date. Preference will be given to candidates who can provide evidence of successful teaching, an active program of research adaptable to student-faculty collaboration, and who have an academic background in psychology. Candidates from underrepresented groups are especially encouraged to apply. Coe’s Psychology Department includes seven full-time faculty and is an integral part of the college’s interdisciplinary Neuroscience major. The Department has a strong commitment to provide intensive, hands-on research experiences and internship placements for its students. A complete application includes: Letter of application Curriculum vitae Teaching & Research statements Unofficial graduate transcript Three letters of recommendation (see note below) Applicants should submit their materials via the link below and request that their recommenders send letters directly to the Office of the Provost at provost@coe.edu. Applicants will be considered complete only when all materials, including letters of recommendation, have been received. Teaching statement: The Coe College Psychology Department is committed to student-centered teaching and mentorship in the liberal arts tradition, and to a learning environment that reflects a wide range of cultural, social, and intellectual perspectives. Please describe your teaching philosophy and background, provide evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., course evaluations), and explain how you would help students from varied backgrounds and levels of preparation succeed through your teaching, mentoring, or other contributions to the department and college. Research statement: The Coe College Psychology Department has a strong tradition in and commitment to collaborative student/faculty research. Please provide a description of the research program that you would bring to or develop at the college. Particular focus should be on describing the role of students as collaborators in your research. For full consideration, all materials, including letters of recommendation, should be received by November 1 .  Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States, as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time.  Successful completion of a background and driver check is required in accordance with Coe College policy. Questions about the position may be directed to Ellen Lee, Associate Professor and Chair of the Psychology Department and Search Committee, at elee@coe.edu. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a7883aca03fc27d01a0632664f9081e": {
      "title": "Constitutional Law Instructor",
      "description": "Position: Constitutional Law Instructor Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1016 # of Openings: 1 The Department of Political Science at Coe College invites applicants for a per-course instructor to teach one of the two courses in our Constitutional Law series.  This position is an excellent fit for graduate students, early-career individuals, and experienced attorneys who are drawn to teaching-focused liberal arts environments. Per-Course Instructor of Constitution Law: The successful candidate will select one course in our Constitutional Law series to teach in Spring 2027 with the opportunity to teach a section of the other course in Spring 2028. The class will be offered 6:30 PM to 9 PM Tuesday nights from January 19 to April 27, 2027. Course options:  There are two courses in the series The Constitution and the Roles of Government This course is an examination of original U.S. court opinions and political writings focusing on the nature and sources of Supreme Court authority; the structure of the US government; judicial review; commerce, taxing, spending, and war powers; with special emphasis upon the separation of powers: the President, Congress, and the Court.  It is open to students with junior and senior standing and is an elective for the political science minor and major. The Constitution and Individual Liberties This course examines original court opinions and political writings focusing on the procedural contents of due process, equal protection under the law, post-Civil War amendments, and civil rights legislation, with special emphasis on freedoms of religion and expression.  It is open to students with junior and senior status and is an elective for the political science minor and major. Qualifications: JD, ABD or terminal degree in Political Science preferred. Experienced attorneys are particularly encouraged to apply. Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States, as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Successful completion of a background and driver check in accordance with Coe College policy. About Coe College and the Department of Political Science: Coe College is a small liberal arts institution in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, where teaching is our central focus. Our students are curious, engaged, and looking for instructors who will meet them as individuals. Small class sizes make genuine mentorship possible, and our faculty take that seriously. The Political Science faculty value student-centered teaching; we prioritize enhancing students’ critical thinking and oral and written communication skills. Many of our majors enter law school soon after graduation. Therefore our Constitutional Law series of courses are important in our curriculum. How to apply: Applications can be submitted at the link below and should include: A current curriculum vitae Unofficial law school or graduate school transcripts Contact information for three professional references Review of the applications will begin on October 9 and will continue until the position is filled. If you have any questions about the course, the students, or what teaching at Coe is like, please contact Kim Lanegran (klanegra@coe.edu) We welcome informal inquiries before you apply and are happy to tell you more. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a7887a19fd3ba90019ffb7964c2633d": {
      "title": "Full-time Adjunct in Chemistry",
      "description": "Position: Full-time Adjunct in Chemistry Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1012 # of Openings: 1 Position Announcement: Full-time Adjunct in Chemistry Coe College invites applications for a full-time adjunct in Chemistry, beginning January 2027. We seek a teacher‑scholar who is passionate about undergraduate education and high‑impact teaching practices. Primary Responsibilities Teach General Chemistry courses with laboratories and other courses aligned with the candidate’s area of expertise/interest Contribute to departmental assessment Hold regular office hours and be responsive to student email questions Qualifications A Ph.D. (preferred; M.S. required) in Chemistry or a closely related field (ABD considered with evidence of timely completion) Demonstrated excellence—or clear potential—for effective, student‑centered undergraduate teaching Ability to teach general chemistry with associated laboratories Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States, as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Successful completion of a background and driver check in accordance with Coe College policy. About the Position This position is a renewable (annually evaluated as college needs require), benefits-eligible appointment with the opportunity for professional growth within a collaborative and student‑focused department. The successful candidate will join a community that values innovative pedagogy, hands‑on learning, and close faculty–student interaction. Application Process Applicants should submit: A cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae or resume Contact information for three references (on request) Applications accepted until the position is filled. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a7883aca0c941c501a0ceaa6cc26a38": {
      "title": "Instructor for Aviation Studies",
      "description": "Position: Instructor for Aviation Studies Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1017 # of Openings: 1 Instructor for Aviation Studies The Department of Business Administration & Economics at Coe College invites applicants for a per-course instructor to teach in our Aviation Studies program. The successful candidate will select one or both of the two following courses to teach in our Spring 2027 semester, January 19 to April 27, 2027. The days/time the course will be offered is negotiable. Course options: Applied Aerodynamics Applied Aerodynamics examines the principles of aerodynamic forces and their impact on aircraft performance and limitations. This course covers a broad spectrum of topics, including longitudinal, lateral, and directional stability and control, as well as low-speed and high-speed aerodynamics. The course also explores how these principles relate to transport design characteristics. Upon successful completion of the course, students will have a solid understanding of aerodynamic principles and their application in the field of aviation. They will be able to analyze and interpret aerodynamic forces and their effects on aircraft performance, stability, control, and design, preparing them for further study or roles within the aerospace industry. Aviation Law Aviation Law provides a strong foundation for understanding the legal and regulatory framework governing civil aviation in the United States legal system, including FAA regulations regarding pilots and flight operations across all certificate levels. The course includes constitutional, administrative, liability, criminal, contract, and international law. It covers topics such as safe operating practices, airport operations, NTSB accident reporting, and procedures in the National Airspace System. Basic principles of tort law and risk management as related to aviation operations and organizations are covered. Qualifications: Candidates with a graduate degree in an applicable field are preferred. Candidates with a bachelor’s degree and significant professional/industry experience demonstrating equivalent competency will also be considered. Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States, as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Successful completion of a background and driver check in accordance with Coe College policy. About Coe College and the Aviation Studies program: Coe College is a small liberal arts institution in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, where teaching is our central focus. Our students are curious, engaged, motivated, and looking for instructors who will meet them as individuals. Small class sizes make genuine mentorship possible, and our faculty take that seriously. The Aviation Studies program is a growing program that values student-centered teaching. Our focus is on providing classroom instruction that helps prepare students for careers as professional pilots or in management positions in the aviation industry. How to apply: Applications can be submitted at the link below and should include: A letter of application A current curriculum vitae College/university transcripts (unofficial) Contact information for three professional references Review of the applications will begin on October 1 and will continue until the position is filled. If you have any questions about the aviation program, the courses, the students, or what teaching at Coe is like, please contact Pam Carstens (pcarstens@coe.edu) We welcome informal inquiries before you apply and are happy to tell you more. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a7887a1983930e9019866d60d525b4c": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach-Athletics",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Coach-Athletics Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1011 # of Openings: 16 Coe College Athletics is looking for enthusiastic and dependable part-time coaches to support our student-athletes and athletic programs. If you enjoy working with college students, have a passion for athletics, and want to be part of a positive team environment, we invite you to apply. Part-time coaching opportunities may vary by sport and season. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a78859ea0f425eb01a0fdecba5215bf": {
      "title": "Student Accounts Manager",
      "description": "Position: Student Accounts Manager Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1021-760152000 # of Openings: 1 Student Accounts Manager Coe College is seeking qualified candidates for the position of Student Accounts Manager. This role oversees all aspects of student accounts receivable, student accounts management, and the collection of Coe loan funds. Responsibilities also include managing online payment systems and providing general accounting support to the Controller and Business Office team. Essential Job Responsibilities: Manage student accounts receivable, including billing, payments, adjustments, refunds, past-due balances, and other account activity. Serve as a primary point of contact for students and families, providing responsive and professional service in person, by phone, and electronically regarding billing, payments, loans, and account questions. Research and resolve student account concerns in collaboration with Financial Aid and other campus offices. Generate and review student billing statements, accounts receivable aging reports, and other reports; reconcile student accounts to the general ledger and provide updates to Finance leadership. Review, post, and reconcile financial aid, private loans, outside scholarships, and other funds applied to student accounts. Manage collection activity for past-due accounts, including student communications and coordination with external collection agencies and loan servicers. Administer and reconcile Coe and applicable federal student loan programs, including required reporting, documentation, and compliance activities. Oversee online payment systems for student accounts and designated College programs. Serve as a School Certifying Official for Veterans Affairs (VA) education benefits and administer the student tuition insurance process. Prepare required student account and loan-related journal entries, reconciliations, reports, and annual IRS Form 1098-T filings. Maintain accurate records in accordance with FERPA, College policies, record-retention requirements, and applicable regulations. Develop, document, and maintain Student Accounts procedures; identify and implement process, system, and customer-service improvements. Assist the Controller with the annual external audit, FISAP reporting, policy review, and other financial reporting requirements. Assist with the supervision and training of student employees and perform other duties and special projects as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in accounting, business, finance or related field required. A minimum of three years of recent related work experience. Personal computer experience in word processing, spreadsheets and database programs – advanced level preferred. Demonstrated ability and willingness to provide direct customer service including sensitive or challenging financial matters. Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Successful completion of a background check in accordance with Coe College policy. Knowledge, Skills and Competencies: Position Specific: Knowledge of relevant federal and state policies, procedures and regulations regarding financial aid and student loan programs. Working knowledge of general accounting, collection methods and common office policies, practices and standard equipment. Interact ethically, professionally and confidentially with diverse groups, faculty, staff and students to develop a deep sense of trust. Exercise professional judgment, insight, problem solving techniques, and independent initiative when applying sound accounting and cash handling policies, procedures and principles. Demonstrate commitment to excellent customer service including the ability to effectively communicate, both orally and in writing. Prepare and maintain records, reports and other documents with an attention to detail and accuracy using a personal computer and data entry skills. Knowledge of the operations, functions, and scope of authority of a college setting or similar environment as related to the handling and disposition of complaints, requests for information, and delegated administrative details. Capacity to organize, manage and prioritize multiple responsibilities, deadlines, tasks and projects while dealing with interruptions and an uneven workload. Ability to maintain positive relationships in a collaborative and diverse team atmosphere. Coe Competencies: Dedication to the educational mission of a private, residential liberal arts college. Ability to maintain positive relationships in a collaborative and diverse team atmosphere. Commitment to excellent customer and/or student service. Demonstrate ethical and responsible decision making. Consistent attendance and accountability necessary to meet position objectives. Every Coe employee shares one mission: to recruit, retain and prepare students for a lifetime of personal and professional success. Working Conditions and Physical Requirements: Typical office setting. Work additional hours, as needed. Coe College is an equal opportunity employer. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a78859f9c72dc92019c95754213731c": {
      "title": "Electrician",
      "description": "Position: Electrician Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 978-7801-53000 # of Openings: 1 Electrician Coe College seeks qualified candidates for the position of Electrician in our Physical Plant Department.  This role, under limited supervision, will apply knowledge and skills of a journey person in the installation, service and repair on a variety of electrical equipment. Will assist in the planning and implementation of the College's maintenance and remodeling projects.  Will perform related work as required. Essential Job Responsibilities: Perform preventative maintenance on all electrical devices as needed within limitations, not to exceed 480 volts. Troubleshoot and repair all electrical and electronic controlled devices using testing equipment such as a volt ohm meter, ammeter, voltmeters, multimeter, etc. Complete work orders as assigned in timely manner Maintain records and submit reports on designated equipment. Perform duties as assigned on the Emergency Response and Control team. Perform other duties as may be assigned. Direct the work of any person assigned to assist. Cooperate with outside contractors. Read and interpret blueprints and drawings.  Keep track of any changes and/or modifications to same, and report them to the Director of the Physical Plant. Cover for plumber and HVAC technician in their absences. For those who have College service vehicles assigned to them. they must maintain a regular maintenance check of the fluid level and keep the vehicle clean (inside and out). Must also track any routine maintenance needs for the vehicle. Will maintain an orderly and clean work shop space Qualifications: High School diploma or equivalency. Must have Journeyman Class B Electrical license. Experience with residential and commercial settings preferred. Must be able to read and interpret mechanical, electrical and structural prints and schematics. Must have a valid Iowa Driver's License. Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Successful completion of a background and driver check in accordance with Coe College policy. Knowledge, Skills and Competencies: Position Specific: Must be neat, clean and show evidence of personal pride in workmanship. Must read and write legibly and follow written and oral instructions. Must have the ability to establish and maintain a good working relationship with Supervisors and fellow workers. For those who have College service vehicles checked out to them, must maintain a regular maintenance check of the fluid levels and keep the vehicle clean. Coe Competencies: Dedication to the educational mission of a private, residential liberal arts college. Ability to maintain positive relationships in a collaborative and diverse team atmosphere. Commitment to excellent customer and/or student service. Demonstrated ethical and responsible decision making. Consistent attendance and accountability necessary to meet position objectives. Alongside the entire Coe community – recruit, retain and prepare Coe students for success. Working Conditions and Physical Requirements: Must be able lift 50+lbs occasionally and/or as needed. May involve exposure to chemical substances, hazards and moving parts. Routine exposure to heat, cold, moisture/wetness, inclement weather, noise air pollution and heights. Work schedule is subject to change in accordance with College needs. Call ins may be mandatory based on College need. Coe College is an equal opportunity employer. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a78839ea13353c501a13643b11c00cb": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Plant or Spatial Ecology",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Plant or Spatial Ecology Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1023 # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Plant or Spatial Ecology Position details : Coe College invites applications from dynamic, student-centered individuals for a full- time tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in the Department of Biology to begin in the Fall of 2027. Primary responsibilities include: Teaching undergraduate courses in Ecology and/or GIS for Biology majors.  Additional rotating duties across semesters would likely also include: designing and teaching both an upper-level elective with lab in the candidate’s field of expertise, as well as teaching the organismal and ecologically-focused lecture with lab, which is part of the sequence for first year biology majors. The ability to teach courses such as Spatial Statistics, Field Botany, Evolution, Invertebrate Biology, Environmental Studies or similar topics is also desirable. When course rotations allow, participation in interdisciplinary and First Year Seminar teaching is also expected. The normal course load typically includes two lecture courses and two labs per semester. Non-teaching responsibilities include student-faculty research, student advising, prospective student recruitment, and committee work. Required Qualifications : Ph.D. in Ecology, Plant Biology, Botany or a related field, with post-doctoral and GIS experience strongly preferred. Demonstrate a commitment to excellent teaching, including the use of inclusive pedagogies along with strong mentoring and academic support of undergraduate student populations of diverse backgrounds. An active research agenda that can be modified for undergraduate research, with a publication record in appropriate scientific journals in the candidate’s field of expertise. Previous experience working with undergraduates is also strongly preferred. Must be currently authorized to work in the United States as Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.  Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Successful completion of a background and drive check in accordance with Coe College policy. The Department is interested in applicants who will complement our commitment to undergraduate education, and who will enhance and expand the expertise and experiences represented through the faculty. This position will grow the Environmental Science side of our department and is open with respect to sub-specialty. https://www.coe.edu/academics/majors-areas-study/biology Department Profile : The Department of Biology offers a Bachelor of Arts degree with concentrations in pre-health, environmental science, molecular biology, or neuroscience also available. The department graduates approximately 35 biology majors per year, making it one of the largest majors on campus. The department also offers courses in service for the college’s nursing and kinesiology programs, as well as for general education. There are 7 full-time faculty with expertise in a wide variety of disciplines, as well as a full-time laboratory manager. Additional faculty and professionals in other departments within the College as well as other nearby research institutions provide excellent opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. Our modern, renovated building (Peterson Hall) is shared with the chemistry and physics departments and contains space for coursework and the College’s natural history collections. The department also houses significant laboratory space that include dissection hoods, a greenhouse, and excellent analytical and molecular equipment. The College’s off-site Wilderness Field Station is located about 12 miles north of Ely, Minnesota in the 2 ½ million-acre Superior National Forest on remote Low Lake. Groups paddle directly by canoe from the field station into the Boundary Waters Canoe Area Wilderness, expanding the field station \"classroom.\" This area is part of the largest and most pristine wilderness area east of the Rocky Mountains. https://www.coe.edu/academics/coe-difference-centers-and-programs/off-campus-study/wilderness-field-station Instructions to Applicants: Submit the following materials online at https://www.coe.edu/why-coe/discover-coe/human-resources/careers/employment-opportunities: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Undergraduate and graduate transcripts Statements on both research interests and teaching philosophy Review of applications will begin on 12/19/2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a7885aca13c11b101a1408f0b6d0c99": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of English",
      "description": "Position: Visiting Assistant Professor of English Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1025 # of Openings: 1 Visiting Assistant Professor of English Position details: The English, Creative Writing, and Communication Studies Department at Coe College invites applications for a two-year, full-time visiting appointment in twentieth- and twenty-first-century Global Anglophone literature to begin August 2027. We seek candidates committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching who can expand our English course offerings as well as support global and interdisciplinary initiatives at the college. Expertise in ethnic American literatures, human rights and literature, or environmental humanities is welcome. The successful candidate will design and teach courses ranging from introductory literature courses to upper-level courses and seminars. The teaching load is six courses per year. This position may be eligible for conversion to a tenure-stream position after two years. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in English or closely related field in hand by August 2027. Demonstrated potential for excellence in the classroom. Evidence of active research agenda and potential for successful scholarly engagement. Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Successful completion of a background check in accordance with Coe College policy. Application Instructions : Applications received before November 13, 2026 will receive full consideration. Please submit the following materials at the link below or online at https://www.coe.edu/why-coe/discover-coe/human-resources/careers/employment-opportunities letter of application curriculum vitae statement of teaching philosophy, with a list of three courses you are prepared to teach at Coe appended to it unofficial graduate transcripts three letters of recommendation (see note below) Applicants should submit their materials via the link above and have letters of recommendation sent directly to the Office of the Provost at provost@coe.edu. Applications will be complete only when all materials, including letters of recommendation, have been received. Coe is committed to fostering a multicultural environment and encourages applications from individuals who will help fulfill that goal. Coe College is an equal opportunity employer. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a78859fa133542101a13ba8ed07318b": {
      "title": "Executive Director/Director of Marketing",
      "description": "Position: Executive Director/Director of Marketing Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1024-771152000 # of Openings: 1 Executive Director/Director of Marketing At Coe College, Coe Makes It Possible is more than a marketing message. It's a reflection of what happens when an ambitious community comes together as One Coe to create opportunities, inspire, and transform lives. As Coe College celebrates 175 years, we're seeking a creative storyteller, strategic thinker, and passionate brand ambassador for the Kohawks. This role is ideal for a driven leader who sees opportunities where others see obstacles, embraces the challenge of elevating a strong brand, and is excited to help tell the stories that embrace our uniqueness. This is more than a content strategy role. It's an opportunity to help shape Coe's future, elevate our brand, and inspire the next generation of Kohawks through compelling stories that reflect the impact of a Coe. You'll collaborate with talented colleagues across campus, help strengthen and steward the Coe brand, and play a key role in advancing institutional priorities during an exciting period of momentum and growth. Along the way, you'll have the opportunity to expand your leadership responsibilities, make a lasting impact on the Coe’s trajectory, and yes, work alongside one of our most recognizable brand ambassadors, Charlie the Kohawk. If you're passionate about storytelling, energized by challenge, and excited by the chance to help guide a historic institution into its next chapter, we'd love to hear from you. After all, Coe Makes It Possible. You Make It Happen. Essential Job Responsibilities: Understand Coe’s existing brand and implement others’ ideas Create and oversee the development of original content and campaigns for marketing avenues including the website, social media, video, media relations, written stories and other materials in a fast-paced setting Tailor content to specific platforms and understand the value of application to a variety of platforms Lead the content development staff in brainstorming and demonstrate continual creativity and brainstorming individually Proactively and independently seek out stories and selling points for marketing use within the office’s overall strategy and goals Serve as direct supervisor for the Content Development Manager and Videographer, and as a member of the Marketing Office’s leadership team Act as a sound decision-maker on preliminary content development and execution Review statistics and third-party publications to produce digestible selling points for the college Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, journalism, writing, communication and a minimum of 4 years of experience in marketing and content development At least one year of experience managing professional staff Exceptional attention to detail Superior communication, listening, writing and proofing skills Ability to effectively juggle multiple projects and priorities at one time Excellent command over written English as well as familiarity with AP Style Higher education and/or sales experience desired but not required Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time Successful completion of a background and driver check in accordance with Coe College policy Knowledge, Skills and Competencies: Position Specific: Strong decision-making skills and judgement Familiarity with social media (Instagram, Snapchat, Twitter, Facebook, LinkedIn) and websites for business use, including an understanding and appreciation for the power of digital marketing Knowledge of the latest technology and marketing trends, and desire to continually expand that knowledge Ability to think in a creative and imaginative way on long- and short-term timelines, and in individual and group settings Ability to excel and deliver high-quality, unique content in high-pressure situations Demonstrated ability to collaborate with people from a wide variety of offices and maintain a positive atmosphere while working under time constraints and deadlines Ability to read quantitative and qualitative data/reports and develop digestible, compelling selling points Naturally flexible and comfortable with shifting gears and pivoting quickly based on the shifting market Coe Competencies: Dedication to the educational mission of a private, residential liberal arts college. Ability to maintain positive relationships in a collaborative and diverse team atmosphere. Commitment to excellent customer and/or student service. Demonstrated ethical and responsible decision making. Consistent attendance and accountability necessary to meet position objectives. Working Conditions and Physical Requirements: Ability to sit or stand for long periods of time and navigate the entire campus. Coe College is an equal opportunity employer. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66ad3d64e016ad629f40d0321&id=8a78839ea150ae2901a15b1a46983b73": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Health & Human Performance",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Health & Human Performance Location: Cedar Rapids, IA Job Id: 1026 # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Health & Human Performance Coe College invites applications from dynamic, student-centered individuals for a full-time tenure-track position of Assistant Professor of Health & Human Performance (formerly Kinesiology) to begin August 2027. The success of Coe College is driven by the success of our graduates. Therefore, we place a priority on recruiting faculty that can fully engage students both in and out of the classroom. The successful candidate should expect to offer high-quality, student-centered instruction at all levels of the curriculum, emphasizing active learning and meaningful student engagement.   All areas of expertise related to Health & Human Performance will be considered, including: Public Health & Health Promotion Sport & Exercise Psychology Exercise Science Pre-Health Professions Exercise Physiology Strength & Conditioning Biomechanics Nutrition Additionally, the successful candidate should demonstrate the ability or willingness to develop and teach courses across multiple modalities, including both online and traditional face-to-face environments. The Department of Health and Human Performance is a collegial and collaborative group of faculty supporting one of Coe College's largest majors. We are committed to providing a student-centered education that integrates disciplinary knowledge, applied learning, and opportunities for personal and professional development. Required Qualifications : Earned Ph.D. or Ed.D. in Health and Human Performance or a closely related field preferred; ABD status considered. Master’s degree in a related discipline accompanied by at least 10 years of relevant practical and higher education teaching experience will also be considered. Demonstrated potential for excellence in the classroom. Potential for scholarly activity that creates opportunities for undergraduate student involvement. Commitment to undergraduate mentoring through formal and informal advising. Must be currently authorized to work in the United States as visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Successful completion of a background and driver check in accordance with Coe College policy. Please submit the following materials online at the link below or at https://www.coe.edu/why-coe/discover-coe/human-resources/careers/employment-opportunities Letter of application Curriculum vitae with documentation of your teaching experience Unofficial copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts Contact information for three professional references (at least one that can speak to your teaching effectiveness). References will only be contacted for candidates that advance in the screening process. Application Instructions : Applications received before January 15th, 2027 will receive full consideration ; review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    }
  },
